{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he shall present from it one from every offering</b> — one whole loaf. It is found that he takes the terumah as four loaves. And I am astonished: when Scripture excluded leaven by the verse \"the offering of first fruits you shall present\" (Leviticus 2:12), why did it not also say \"and the offering of the todah\"? But this is no question, for Scripture said \"and upon the altar they shall not ascend for a pleasing fragrance,\" and from the bread of the todah nothing at all goes upon the altar, since it only requires waving. And even though they said (Menahot 57a) concerning the showbread that one transgresses through its leavening, because the frankincense upon it — which belongs to the bread as a remembrance — is an offering by fire to YHWH, but from the bread of the todah nothing at all goes upon the altar. And perhaps Scripture did not need that exclusion except on account of honey, since it was not specified concerning first fruits that they may come from honey, and it included leaven with it, and said concerning both of them \"the offering of first fruits you shall present them.\" But concerning leaver explicitly stated in its own place there is no need to specify it, for Scripture does not state in \"whoever profanes it shall be put to death\" (Exodus 31:14) an exception for the sacrificial service, nor in \"the nakedness of your brother's wife\" (Leviticus 18:16) an exception for the yevamah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The verse citation שמות לא י\"ד is rendered as Exodus 31:14; the text reads מחלליה (profanes it) referring to Shabbat. The word שאור here means leaven/sourdough."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:21.931138696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}